; A misspelled keyword beneath a commodity or account directive is an
; error, whether or not the line carries an argument and whatever the
; checking level (issue #3260).  A misspelling that carried an argument
; used to be discarded without a word, so the intended format or check
; never took effect, while the same misspelling without one was reported
; as a known directive missing its argument.

commodity $
    formt  $1,000.00
    nomarket

commodity EUR
    formt

account Assets:Cash
    nte     Petty cash
    chek    amount > 0

account Expenses:Food
    chek    amount > 0

2024-01-01 Payee
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Assets:Cash

test bal -> 4
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 9:
Error: Unrecognized commodity directive 'formt'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 13:
Error: Unrecognized commodity directive 'formt'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
Error: Unrecognized account directive 'nte'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 20:
Error: Unrecognized account directive 'chek'
end test

test --pedantic bal -> 4
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 9:
Error: Unrecognized commodity directive 'formt'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 13:
Error: Unrecognized commodity directive 'formt'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
Error: Unrecognized account directive 'nte'
While parsing file "$FILE", line 20:
Error: Unrecognized account directive 'chek'
end test
